<title>SWEDEN: Enskilda lowers trading view on H&amp;M.</title>
<headline>Enskilda lowers trading view on H&amp;M.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish brokerage house Enskilda Fondkommission on Friday said it had lowered its trading recommendation on Swedish fashion retailer Hennes &amp; Mauritz to a 'reduce' from an 'outperform'.</p>
<p>&quot;The share has been really good and has reached such a level that we were forced to change our recommendation,&quot; said an analyst at Enskilda, the brokerage arm of S-E-Banken.</p>
<p>H&amp;M shares have soared over the past year, rising over 150 percent in 1996, and hitting an all-time high of 1,070 crowns this week amid rumours of a share split and ahead of Q4 earnings on January 30.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
